[["wrb.fr",null,"[null,[\"c_1ee83e8501ea6bc0\",\"r_ac2fa738c07495a6\"],null,null,[[\"rc_39569488f1a7d2ee\",[\"Expert predictions for SpaceX’s valuation heading into the end of 2026 center around an **$800 billion to $1.5 trillion** range, with consensus clustering around the **$1.0T to $1.3T** mark depending on market liquidity and whether valuation is measured via private secondary transactions or implied public-market targets. \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Valuation Snapshot \\u0026 Expert Ranges\\n\\n| Scenario | Implied Valuation | Key Drivers / Valuation Basis |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Bear Case** | **$580B – $800B** | Grounded in secondary market tender levels (~$800B); assumes margin compression on Starlink and multiple compression toward industrial/defense comps (12x–15x sales). |\\n| **Base / Consensus Case** | **$1.0T – $1.3T** | Strong recurring Starlink cash flow (~$15B–$20B run-rate) paired with continued commercial launch dominance; valued at 20x–25x forward revenue. |\\n| **Bull Case** | **$1.5T – $2.0T+** | High-end Wall Street projections pricing SpaceX as an orbital infrastructure and telecommunications monopoly, assuming rapid Starship commercialization and direct-to-cell scaling. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Upside Catalysts\\n\\n* **Starlink Unit Economics \\u0026 Direct-to-Cell Expansion:** Starlink's recurring subscriber revenue forms the bedrock of modern SpaceX valuation models. Rapid enterprise adoption (aviation, maritime) and monetization of direct-to-cell telecom partnerships provide high-margin, scalable software/telecom multiples rather than lower aerospace hardware multiples.\\n* **Starship Reusability \\u0026 Payload Capacity:** Full operational deployment of Starship dramatically reduces cost-per-kilogram to orbit. This unlocks massive margin expansion for deploying next-gen Starlink satellites and captures higher-margin deep-space and NASA Artemis mission revenue.\\n* **Defense \\u0026 National Security Moat:** Starshield expansion and high-priority government intelligence contracts guarantee stable, long-dated federal cash flows with minimal competition.\\n* **Public Market Liquidity Premium:** Continued preparations or structural carve-outs ahead of potential public listings create heightened institutional demand and liquidity premiums relative to traditional private market discounts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Downside Risks\\n\\n* **Starship Regulatory and Technical Bottlenecks:** Delays in full orbital reusability, Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) environmental review hurdles, or high capital expenditure burn rates from testing could weigh heavily on near-term cash generation.\\n* **Low Earth Orbit (LEO) Spectrum \\u0026 Geopolitical Pushback:** Intensified scrutiny over orbital congestion, space debris mitigation, and foreign sovereignty concerns regarding sovereign satellite internet deployment could impede Starlink’s international addressable market.\\n* **Emerging LEO Mega-Constellation Competition:** Accelerating deployments by rival constellations (such as Amazon’s Project Kuiper or state-backed initiatives) could spark pricing pressure on broadband bandwidth, eroding Starlink's average revenue per user (ARPU).\\n* **Multiples Compression:** Valuations above $1 trillion implicitly treat SpaceX as a high-margin tech and telecom platform. Any broad macro risk-off sentiment or a pivot by analysts toward treating capital-intensive space operations as industrial manufacturing could trigger significant multiple contraction.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Sources\\n* [ThinkMarkets: SpaceX Valuation \\u0026 IPO Analysis](https://www.thinkmarkets.com/en/trading-academy/market-events/spacex-ipo-2026-date-spacex-valuation-and-proxy-share-cfds/)\\n* [SatNews: SpaceX Valuation in Secondary Sale \\u0026 IPO Horizons](https://satnews.com/2025/12/06/spacex-targets-800-billion-valuation-in-secondary-sale-eyes-2026-ipo/)\\n* [Sacra: SpaceX Financial Breakdown \\u0026 Valuation Scenarios](https://sacra.com/c/spacex/valuation/)\\n* [Morningstar: SpaceX Valuation Overview](https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/does-spacexs-sky-high-valuation-make-sense)\"],[null,[[[\"Expert predictions for SpaceX’s valuation heading into the end of 2026 center around an **$800 billion to $1.5 trillion** range, with consensus clustering around the **$1.0T to $1.3T** mark depending on market liquidity and whether valuation is measured via private secondary transactions or implied public-market targets.\",null,null,[[0,324],[0,322]]],[1],[[\"https://www.thinkmarkets.com/en/trading-academy/market-events/spacex-ipo-2026-date-spacex-valuation-and-proxy-share-cfds/\",\"SpaceX Valuation 2026: Latest Figures, IPO Date \\u0026 How to Trade\",\"https://encrypted-tbn3.gstatic.com/favicon-tbn?q\\u003dtbn%3AANd9GcT-sR04KU7D4IGOqomIk8QdoXu3kZFnNPhx0j4VwsqtWbX_8CoFBTOOuSLqszwrN4O2bAt1LWVWnT6y6kWQ0W4-ZK9QJrv1ObkLbI_DM-4_\",\"December 2025: $800 billion (private tender offer); Early 2026: ~$1.5 \\ntrillion (Secondary market reports); 2026 IPO (June): priced at a valuation \\nof\",[[\"Expert predictions for SpaceX’s valuation heading into the end of 2026 center around an **$800 billion to $1.5 trillion** range, with consensus clustering around the **$1.0T to $1.3T** mark depending on market liquidity and whether valuation is measured via private secondary transactions or implied public-market targets.\",null,null,[[0,324],[0,322]]]],null,\"ThinkMarkets\",9,\"\"]],\"spp_6a70d31a2f9e4f13\"],[[\"Starlink's recurring subscriber revenue forms the bedrock of modern SpaceX valuation models.\",null,null,[[1185,1277],[1171,1263]]],[1],[[\"https://satnews.com/2025/12/06/spacex-targets-800-billion-valuation-in-secondary-sale-eyes-2026-ipo/#:~:text\\u003dThe%20valuation%20leap%20is%20underpinned%20by%20the,estimated%20between%20%2412%20billion%20and%20%2415%20billion.\",\"SpaceX Targets $800 Billion Valuation in Secondary Sale, Eyes\",\"https://encrypted-tbn1.gstatic.com/favicon-tbn?q\\u003dtbn%3AANd9GcTqQXKdYkUwBhssB7HADrk-P5q0i_3dp0